# Play Console → App content → Privacy policy URL:
# https://loopgallery.a-u.us/privacy

# Android Google Sign-In (recommended — native account picker in the APK):
# 1. Firebase Console → Project settings → Your apps → Add Android app
#    Package: us.a_u.loopgallery.app
# 2. Download google-services.json → mobile/android/app/google-services.json
# 3. Add SHA-1 fingerprints in Firebase (Auth → Google must be enabled):
#    Debug:  keytool -list -v -keystore ~/.android/debug.keystore -alias androiddebugkey -storepass android
#    Play:   Play Console → App integrity → App signing key certificate → SHA-1
# 4. npm run mobile:sync && rebuild APK (npm run mobile:apk or Play release)
#
# Without google-services.json the app falls back to Chrome Custom Tab OAuth
# (/auth/mobile → /auth/complete). App Links must verify (assetlinks.json SHA-256).

# Play upload signing (for .aab uploads — separate from Firebase / assetlinks):
#   Upload key SHA-1:  Play Console → App integrity → Upload key certificate
#   App signing SHA-256: assetlinks.json + Firebase (what users install)
#   Find upload keystore: bash mobile/scripts/find-upload-keystore.sh ~/fore ~/Downloads
#   Then: mobile/android/keystore.properties + npm run mobile:release

# Point the WebView at a different host (default: https://loopgallery.a-u.us)
# CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL=https://loopgallery.a-u.us

# Android emulator → dev machine (run `npm run dev` at repo root first)
# CAPACITOR_SERVER_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000
